WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.480
Young people have earned a reputation for
taking down industries and institutions,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.139
from Applebee's to breakfast cereal. And
although many of these critiques are

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:18.500
exaggerated, the effect that young people
have had on organized religion is indisputable.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.100
More than four-in-ten young people
are religiously unaffiliated today.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.440
It is the most common
religious identity among young adults.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.500
And a new survey suggests that these
religious changes may be permanent.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.380
And here's a couple of reasons why: First,
young people today were raised in less

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.220
religious homes. Growing up, they were
less likely to attend religious services,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.340
say grace over dinner,
or go to Sunday school. The young adults

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.800
who've left their childhood religion are also
leaving early — mostly during adolescence.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.510
In fact, 70% report having become religiously

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:52.600
unaffiliated before they turned 18.
So, a 30-year old who is unaffiliated

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.910
today has likely been that way for
over a decade. Finally, due to the

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.640
rise of online dating and the sheer
number of secular romantic partners,

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:07.060
secular couples have now become more
common, reinforcing secular identity and beliefs.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.800
Did you have a religious
upbringing? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.880
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.659
and be sure to LIKE subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

